SUMMARY:Deadline: NBER i3: Open Data Fellows Program 2027
DESCRIPTION:The fourth cohort of the NBER Innovation Information Initiative
  (i3) Open Data Fellows supports graduate students building public dataset
 s\, tools\, code or metadata for research on innovation and entrepreneursh
 ip.\n\nOrganisation: National Bureau of Economic Research (NBER)\, Innovat
 ion Information Initiative (i3)\nLocation: United States (NBER\, Cambridge
 \, MA)\; international applicants welcome\, including those on US student 
 visas (payment may be affected\, check with your international student off
 ice)\nAward: USD 1\,500 per fellow\, at least five fellowships\, plus trav
 el reimbursement to present at the i3 Technical Working Group meeting in D
 ecember 2027. No application fee.\nDuration: 12 months (January to Decembe
 r 2027)\n\nMore: https://www.nber.org/calls-papers-and-proposals/open-data
 -fellows-program-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://www.nber.org/calls-papers-and-proposals/open-data-fellows-progr
 am-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States (NBER\, Cambridge\, MA)\; international applicants w
 elcome\, including those on US student visas (payment may be affected\, ch
 eck with your international student office)
END:VEVENT
